    "comparisons": {
      "confound": "The unexposed arm also trained on 48 fewer studies (3,478 vs 3,526) and selected over 433 rather than 441. Dropping training data can only hurt, so a null needs no control; only a drop does. See the protocol.",
      "primary": "exposed/uniform_mean_768 versus unexposed/uniform_mean_768, paired over the same 56 studies, the same folds and the same study resamples, via scripts/compare_downstream_arms.py. Pre-registered: unexposed at or above exposed means exposure did not materially inflate 0.7105; unexposed materially below means every probe figure in digest/ needs relabelling.",
